## Langfuse adds Gemini decision models to evaluators

Source: Langfuse — https://langfuse.com/changelog/2026-11-13-gemini-decision-model-evaluators
Published: 2026-11-13
Channel: news

Langfuse is an AI observability and evaluation platform that records and scores application behavior. Its decision-model evaluators can now use Google’s Gemini Decisions API. First, select a Google AI Studio connection and the supported decision model in the evaluator. Then configure a Choice, Score, or Yes / no question. Each question writes a score with its probabilities and confidence.

The announcement suggests checking answers against a refund policy, routing conversations for review, or grading helpfulness against a rubric. Google bills input tokens only for these decisions. Vertex AI connections are not yet supported for this evaluation integration.

Why it matters: Teams testing this evaluator should use Google AI Studio credentials and validate its decisions on their own rubric before relying on the saved confidence values.

